328:### D-I â€” Surface marks. AMENDED per gate-1 ruling 1: .13 is `ui`.
329:The wiring leaf re-runs the ui-tagged subset of *"the auth screens (signup, sign-in,
330:verification, reset)"* â€” the `ui` mark is the mechanism by which that leaf finds its work.
331:AT-001.38 (`ui`) is the sign-in screen's negative; AT-001.14 (`ui`) is the reset screen.
332:AT-001.12 is `backend`: expiry and revocation are the session layer's enforcement, and no
333:named screen carries them. **AT-001.13 is `ui`**, and the reason is the mark's mechanism, not
334:a screen: the one clause only a wired client can make true â€” "automatically", the client SDK
335:scheduling the refresh â€” needs a dev-board owner, and a `backend` mark would orphan it until
336:the requirement's far-away integration-tier gate (the gate-1 reviewer's finding, accepted).
337:The wired re-run drives .13 through the wired client, where supabase-js's automatic refresh
338:is the thing under test; the loop-tier body proves this leaf's half â€” refresh works, takes no
339:credentials, and an unrefreshed sibling of the same instant dies. The mark leans on the wired
340:client rather than on one named screen, and this sentence is the honest record of that.
