12:burying it. **ACCEPTED.** Handing the whole body to the pure module requires reading the body
13:before the status short-circuits, so the parse must not throw; the executor made it
14:non-throwing and `null`-on-failure, which keeps every refusal path byte-for-byte identical â€”
15:including an Auth outage answering HTML, which stays a 401. The one changed edge â€” 2xx plus
16:unparseable body â€” moves from 502 to a refusal, which is the fail-closed direction and matches
17:the module's stated promise. It is not reachable through GoTrue itself (JSON on both
18:branches). Preserving the old 502 exactly would need a status check in `edge.ts`, a second
19:copy of the 2xx rule outside the module â€” the exact defect the extraction removes. The plan's
20:D-B now records the accepted edge.
