91: * exact about why this function does not look at the token. Auth decides whether a token is live:
92: * a revoked session, an expired access token, a signature that does not verify and a token for a
93: * deleted user all come back as a refusal status. This module never parses a token, never reads an
94: * expiry claim, and holds no clock â€” so there is no second opinion here to drift from Auth's.
95: *
96: * THE HANDLE IS DERIVED, NOT PASSED IN. `extractGithubHandle` is given the WHOLE body rather than a
97: * pre-narrowed field, for the reason its own header gives: the judgement about what counts as a
98: * linked GitHub identity has one home. This matters more since the extraction moved out of
99: * `edge.ts`, because the bridge left behind is untyped â€” a delegation that handed this function
100: * `{ id }` instead of the complete body would return a caller with `githubHandle: null` and refuse
101: * every linked volunteer at the deployed edge. `loop/items/AI4DEV-60/proof-local.ts` check (g) is
102: * the live control that fails on exactly that mistake.
103: *
104: * A BLANK `id` IS ACCEPTED, and that is stated rather than left to be discovered. `''` is a string,
105: * so it passes â€” which is what `resolveCaller` did before this module existed, and this refactor
106: * preserves the deployed behaviour rather than tightening it. Nothing turns on it: GoTrue answers a
107: * uuid, and an empty id reaching `public.complete_signup` fails the database's own `uuid` cast. A
108: * leaf that wants blank refused should say so as a decision, not acquire it as a side effect of
109: * moving code.
